<div class="help-layout__content">
<div class="placeholder-notice" role="note" id="placeholder-notice">
  <p><%= t("nexus_ccs.debias.page.placeholder_html") %></p>
</div>

<section class="help-section" id="our-approach" aria-labelledby="h-our-approach">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-our-approach">Our approach</h2>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">The University's collections include Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander material and material from the colonial era. Many records were written by people in the past, in the words of their time. Some of those words are now considered offensive, inaccurate or outdated, and some were never respectful. <span data-placeholder>[Placeholder: the collections team and Indigenous advisers to write the University's approach.]</span></p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">The collections team keeps a list of words and phrases to look out for, and reviews it with Indigenous advisers. <span data-placeholder>[Placeholder: who owns the list, how often it is reviewed, and how terms are chosen.]</span> This page also sits beside the <a href="<%= help_path(anchor: "indigenous") %>">cultural protocols that apply to Indigenous records</a>.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="help-section" id="how-the-notice-works" aria-labelledby="h-how-the-notice-works">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-how-the-notice-works">How the notice works</h2>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">When a record's title, description, subjects, places or other details contain a word or phrase from the list, the record page shows a notice near the title. The notice names the term, shows it in the words around it, and explains why it may be offensive or outdated. Where the record shows the term, it is marked, and a screen reader says "flagged term" before it. A <strong>Caution</strong> means the term may cause offence or distress. A <strong>Note</strong> means it is outdated or imprecise.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">A computer program matches the list against the text, whole words only. It can miss a term that is spelt differently, and it cannot tell when a flagged word is used respectfully, in a quotation, or for a different meaning. A record without a notice may still contain language that some people find offensive.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="help-section" id="original-wording" aria-labelledby="h-original-wording">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-original-wording">Why we show the original wording</h2>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">Terms are shown as they appear in the original catalogue records. We do not change or hide the words in a record: that would hide how the collection was described, and make it harder to find and to correct. The notice sits beside the words instead. Searching for a term still finds the records that use it.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="help-section" id="suggest-a-correction" aria-labelledby="h-suggest-a-correction">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-suggest-a-correction">Suggest a correction</h2>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">If a record uses a term that should carry a notice, a notice is wrong or unhelpful, or you can suggest better wording, tell the collection team. On the record page, use <strong>Contact the collection team</strong>: the message starts with the record's details. For anything else, see <a href="<%= help_path(anchor: "contact-us") %>">Contact Us</a>. <span data-placeholder>[Placeholder: what happens to a suggestion, and how long a reply takes.]</span></p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
</div>
</div>
</main>
